      "content": "It sounds like you are navigating a massive identity crisis following a significant shift in purpose. When a central part of your life, like competition, defined your \"self,\" the void it leaves can feel like a complete erasure of who you were. This feeling of waiting for yourself to return is a common part of deep transitional periods. Be gentle with yourself as you explore who exists beneath that former definition.",
      "source": "target",
