    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but what if there is nothing beneath? i've tried looking for some other version of me, but there's nothing there. it's like the story ended when the injury happened. i'm just some extra pages at the end of a book that's already been closed. it feels so pointless to just keep dragging this empty shell around when the person who actually lived is gone.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable to feel that the story has ended when something so vital to your identity was lost. However, the story doesn't automatically end; it often changes genre after a major turning point. Even if the powerful, focused \"you\" isn't immediately visible, there is a capacity for a new narrative to begin. Perhaps the current void is simply the necessary quiet before a new kind of self can start to be written.",
      "source": "target",
